\widctlpar\fi-360\li1176\sa160\sl252\slmult1\b0\fs36 What is the first step in the troubleshooting process?\par

\pard\widctlpar\li816\sa160\sl252\slmult1\f1\fs22\'e0\f0\fs36  b) \b Identifying the problem\b0  \par
2)\fs22  \fs36 Which of the following tools is commonly used to diagnose hardware issues by testing electrical connections?\par
\f1\'e0\f0  c\b ) Multi meter\b0  \par
3)\fs22  \fs36 Which of the following best describes the purpose of a VPN (Virtual Private Network)?\par
\f1\'e0\f0  a\b ) Encrypting network traffic to prevent eavesdropping\b0\par
4) Which Windows utility can be used to view system logs, monitor performance, and diagnose hardware and software issues? \par
\f1\'e0\b\f0 Event Viewer\b0  \par
\b\fs44 Section-2\par
\b0\fs36 5) Safe Mode is a diagnostic mode in Windows that loads only essential system services and drivers, allowing users to troubleshoot and fix problems with the operating system.\par
\f1\'e0\b\f0 True\par
\b0 6)\fs22  \fs36  A system restore point is a snapshot of the computer's system files, registry, and configuration settings at a specific point in time, which can be used to revert the system to a previous state if problems occur.\par
\f1\'e0\b\f0 True\b0\par
7)\fs22  \fs36  Ping is a command-line utility used to test network connectivity by sending ICMP echo requests to a target device and waiting for ICMP echo replies.\par
\f1\'e0\b\f0 True\par
\fs44\par
Section-3\par
\b0\fs36 8)\fs22  \fs36 Describe the steps involved in troubleshooting a computer that fails to boot into the operating system.\par
\f1\'e0\f0 Here are few steps:\par
          1) \b Check Power and Connections:\b0\line Make sure the computer turns on, cables are plugged in, and the monitor works.\par
          2) \b Look for Error Messages:\b0\line Pay attention to any messages or beeping sounds during startup.\par
          3) \b Open BIOS/UEFI Settings:\b0\line Press a key like F2 or DEL when starting up to check that the computer detects the hard drive and the boot order is correct.\par
            4)\b Try Safe Mode:\b0\line Restart and press F8 (or follow steps for your system) to boot into Safe Mode to see if the computer works with basic settings.\par
            5) \b Use Repair Tools:\b0\line Use Startup Repair or System Restore if available to fix boot issues.\par
            6)\b Check Hardware:\b0\line Run tools to test your RAM, hard drive, and other hardware, or try replacing faulty parts.\par
             7)\b Reinstall Windows:\par
\b0 reinstall the operating system, but back up your files first if possible.\par
